# Go (WiChat backend)

## Tests live under `test/`

Put test files in a **`test/` subdirectory** next to the code under test — not as `*_test.go` siblings in the production package folder.

```text
wi-shared/exception/
  kind.go
  error.go
  test/
    error_test.go
    kind_test.go
```

- Test package name: **`{pkgname}_test`** only (e.g. `service_test`). Production packages: **lowercase** per Effective Go (see `wichat-go-style.mdc`); not camelCase (`serviceTest`, `authHttp`).
- Import the module under test; tests are **black-box** (exported API only).
- Run: `go test ./...` from the module root (includes `.../test` packages).

**Exception:** tiny white-box tests for unexported helpers — only when unavoidable; keep in `test/` still, or document why a single in-package file is required.

## Formatting and lint

- Format with **gofumpt** and **goimports** (via `golangci-lint fmt`); each module has its own `.golangci.yml` (e.g. `backend/ms-user/.golangci.yml`).
- Before opening a PR: `cd backend/<module> && make check` (e.g. `ms-user`, `api-gateway`, `wi-shared`).
- Local dev: `cd backend && make dev-ms-user` / `make dev-api-gateway` (Air), or `make run-*` without reload; see `backend/Makefile`.
- gRPC contracts: edit `backend/wi-shared/models/**.proto`; run `make proto` from `wi-shared/`; never hand-edit `models/gen/`.
- In `Run(ctx)` and server goroutines: return errors to `main` — no `log.Fatalf` in listeners.

## No re-exports

Do not create proxy packages or files that re-export another package’s API (`var ErrFoo = constants.ErrFoo`, `type T = othertype.T` across packages, barrel `errors.go` shims). Import the defining package. Details: `wichat-go-layers.mdc` § “No re-exports”.

## ms-user repository split (do not regress)

- `internal/user/repository` — users, groups, instance policy, Google identity rows.
- `internal/auth/repository` — sessions/refresh Postgres; Redis OTP/password-reset stores.
- Shared sentinels: `pkg/constants`; PG row/unique mapping: `pkg/db` (`pgErr`). Group other helpers under flat `pkg/<role>/` (see `ms-user/pkg/README.md`).
- Auth `service.NewService` takes **two** `PgRepository` deps (`userrepo`, `authrepo`), not one combined repo.
- **Mocks:** only Postgres under `internal/<domain>/repository/mock/` (`pg_repository_mock.go`). Redis tests use **miniredis** + production store constructors — no `repository/mock` for Redis (`wichat-go-layers.mdc`).
- **Service:** one `service.go` per `internal/<domain>/service/`; tests only `service/test/service_test.go`; split domains (`auth`, `user`, `group`) not extra files in one package (`wichat-go-layers.mdc`).

